{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "def sort_third(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three, while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a copy of the list to ensure the original input is not modified.\n    result_list = list(l)\n\n    # Collect elements and their original indices that are divisible by three.\n    elements_to_sort = []\n    indices_to_sort = []\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            elements_to_sort.append(l[i])\n            indices_to_sort.append(i)\n\n    # Sort the collected elements in ascending order.\n    sorted_elements = sorted(elements_to_sort)\n\n    # Place the sorted elements back into their original positions in the new list.\n    sorted_elements_iterator = iter(sorted_elements)\n    for i in indices_to_sort:\n        result_list[i] = next(sorted_elements_iterator)\n\n    return result_list"}
