{"task_id": "HumanEval/39", "solution": "```python\ndef prime_fib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    prime_fib returns n-th number that is a Fibonacci number and it's also prime.\n    >>> prime_fib(1)\n    2\n    >>> prime_fib(2)\n    3\n    >>> prime_fib(3)\n    5\n    >>> prime_fib(4)\n    13\n    >>> prime_fib(5)\n    89\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Per CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS, do not raise exceptions for invalid n.\n    # Assume n is a positive integer.\n\n    # Handle the first prime Fibonacci number as a special case.\n    if n == 1:\n        return 2\n\n    def _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a number is prime using trial division.\"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        if num == 2 or num == 3:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n    a, b = 0, 1  # Initialize Fibonacci sequence (F(0), F(1))\n    prime_count = 0\n\n    # Advance the Fibonacci sequence past 0, 1, 1, as these are not prime or handled.\n    # The first Fibonacci number to check for primality is 2 (F(3)).\n    # Call next_fib three times to get to the state where 'a' is 2.\n    # 1. fib_num = 0, next state (1, 1)\n    _ = a\n    a, b = b, a + b\n    # 2. fib_num = 1, next state (1, 2)\n    _ = a\n    a, b = b, a + b\n    # 3. fib_num = 1, next state (2, 3)\n    _ = a\n    a, b = b, a + b\n\n    while True:\n        current_fib = a  # Current Fibonacci number to check\n        a, b = b, a + b  # Generate the next Fibonacci number for the subsequent iteration\n\n        if _is_prime(current_fib):\n            prime_count += 1\n            if prime_count == n:\n                return current_fib\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "def triples_sum_to_zero(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    triples_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    it returns True if there are three distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    # Sort the list to enable the two-pointer technique.\n    nums = sorted(l)\n\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        # Skip duplicate elements for 'i' to avoid redundant checks.\n        if i > 0 and nums[i] == nums[i-1]:\n            continue\n\n        left, right = i + 1, n - 1\n        while left < right:\n            current_sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right]\n\n            if current_sum == 0:\n                return True\n            elif current_sum < 0:\n                left += 1\n            else: # current_sum > 0\n                right -= 1\n    return False"}
