{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "```python\ndef encode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns an encoded string by shifting each lowercase English alphabet character by 5 positions.\n    Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged, with wrap-around from 'z' to 'a'.\n    \"\"\"\n    SHIFT_AMOUNT = 5\n    ALPHABET_SIZE = 26\n    ORD_A = ord('a')\n    encoded_chars = []\n    for ch in s:\n        if 'a' <= ch <= 'z':\n            shifted_ord = ((ord(ch) - ORD_A + SHIFT_AMOUNT) % ALPHABET_SIZE) + ORD_A\n            encoded_chars.append(chr(shifted_ord))\n        else:\n            encoded_chars.append(ch)\n    return \"\".join(encoded_chars)\n\n\ndef decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string previously encoded by encode_shift, returning the original string.\n    Each lowercase English alphabet character is shifted backward by 5 positions, wrapping from 'a' to 'z'.\n    \"\"\"\n    SHIFT_AMOUNT = 5\n    ALPHABET_SIZE = 26\n    ORD_A = ord('a')\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for ch in s:\n        if 'a' <= ch <= 'z':\n            shifted_ord = ((ord(ch) - ORD_A - SHIFT_AMOUNT + ALPHABET_SIZE) % ALPHABET_SIZE) + ORD_A\n            decoded_chars.append(chr(shifted_ord))\n        else:\n            decoded_chars.append(ch)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)\n```"}
