{"task_id": "HumanEval/64", "solution": "```python\ndef vowels_count(s):\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of vowels in a string.\n    'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u' are always vowels. 'y' is a vowel only when it is at the end of the word.\n    \"\"\"\n    VOWELS_SET = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n    vowel_count = 0\n    lower_word = s.lower()\n    word_length = len(lower_word)\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(lower_word):\n        if char in VOWELS_SET:\n            vowel_count += 1\n        elif char == 'y' and i == word_length - 1:\n            vowel_count += 1\n    return vowel_count\n```"}
